For the knee-flexor route, the pulley variant converged to a collision-feasible layout with zero bound violations and a peak predicted flexion torque of \qty{85.56}{
ewton\meter} on the insertion-side measure, the torque applied at the insertion after the tackle's force loss. At unity transmission, the knee-flexor pulley route increased peak predicted knee-axis torque from \qty{81.23}{
ewton\meter} to \qty{85.74}{
ewton\meter}, while limiting off-axis torque to \qty{0.803}{
ewton\meter}. This comparison measures the effect of the two optimized routing configurations; their different objective functions do not isolate the pulley alone. The pulley serves as a redirect in this configuration rather than a force multiplier.

