ewton\meter}. The OpenSim model retains its eight original moving-path-point vias for rectus-femoris and vastii patella tracking; the candidate pulley routes were not added to those paths, and the model contains no pulley entities. The MuJoCo conversion used for the simulation work predates this attachment update and the pulley batch. Physical tests of the redesigned knee routes are reported in Section~ef{sec:redesign_physical}.

Ground contact is disabled and measured foot forces are zero. The adopted stage-2 suspension statistic is \qty{99.860}{\percent}, calculated from \qty{768.662}{
ewton} mean spring force over \qtyrange{5}{16}{\second} using the legacy total model mass of \qty{78.4646}{\kilogram} and weight of \qty{769.737726}{
ewton}. That mass includes a separate fixed \qty{0.1}{\kilogram} ground body. The aligned-recording metadata instead uses the pelvis subtree, \qty{78.3646}{\kilogram} or \qty{768.756726}{
ewton}; dividing the same legacy force samples by that denominator gives \qty{99.9877}{\percent}. The adopted percentage is retained with its original denominator. Figure~ef{fig:sns_biw2l_air} displays unnormalized force in newtons. The legacy samples are tagged at interval start, while aligned states are tagged at interval end, so an independently selected aligned window must also retain its own timestamps. These measures characterize suspension, with frontal guidance retained, rather than a minimum ground-walking support requirement. Higher-expression trials stopped at the predictive knee-extension guard; the completed condition retains the guard and does not clip joint state. This controller has not completed standing or ground stages.

The selected condition completed \qty{28}{\second}. During $16\leq t<28$\,s, mean vertical harness force was \qty{570.20625}{
ewton}, or \qty{77.5}{\percent} of the \qty{735.75}{
ewton} weight of the \qty{75}{\kilogram} model. Seven right and six left qualifying unloaded-clear intervals produced twelve alternations. Each interval required whole-foot mesh clearance above \qty{5}{\milli\meter}, ipsilateral normal load below \qty{7.36}{
ewton}, contralateral load above \qty{15}{
ewton}, and duration of at least \qty{80}{\milli\second}. The retained every-\qty{2}{\milli\second} knee-bound accumulator reports whole-trial minimum flexion of \ang{11.20} on the right and \ang{5.10} on the left, against a \ang{1} guard. The saved \qty{10}{\milli\second} traces are a different sampling interval and do not independently reconstruct every physics-step extremum. The \qty{-74.7}{\milli\meter} world-forward displacement describes guided stepping approximately in place. Orientation and lateral guidance remained active.
